  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given MMM triplets (X1,Y1,B1),(X2,Y2,B2),…,(XM,YM,BM)(X_1, Y_1, B_1), (X_2, Y_2, B_2), \\ldots, (X_M, Y_M, B_M)(X1​,Y1​,B1​),(X2​,Y2​,B2​),…,(XM​,YM​,BM​). Find the number of sequences of positive integers A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​ such that for each valid iii, lcm(AXi,AYi)=Bi\\mathrm{lcm}(A_{X_i},A_{Y_i}) = B_ilcm(AXi​​,AYi​​)=Bi​, or determine that there is an infinite number of such sequences.\n\nSince the answer can be very large, compute it modulo 1,000,000,0071,000,000,0071,000,000,007 (109+710^9 + 7109+7). Note that the values B1,B2,…,BMB_1, B_2, \\ldots, B_MB1​,B2​,…,BM​ can also be very large ― you are given their prime decompositions.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤31 \\le T \\le 31≤T≤3",
      "0≤M≤1040 \\le M \\le 10^40≤M≤104",
      "1≤N≤381 \\le N \\le 381≤N≤38",
      "1≤Xi,Yi≤N1 \\le X_i, Y_i \\le N1≤Xi​,Yi​≤N for each valid iii",
      "0≤Ri≤2000 \\le R_i \\le 2000≤Ri​≤200 for each valid iii",
      "prp_rpr​ is a prime for each valid rrr",
      "pr≤106p_r \\le 10^6pr​≤106 for each valid rrr",
      "the total number of different primes prp_rpr​ in each test case does not exceed 555",
      "1≤er≤1061 \\le e_r \\le 10^61≤er​≤106 for each valid rrr",
      "Subtasks**Subtask #1 (20 points, time limit 2 seconds):** N≤20N \\le 20N≤20",
      "**Subtask #2 (35 points, time limit 4 seconds):** N≤30N \\le 30N≤30",
      "**Subtask #3 (45 points, time limit 4.5 seconds):** T=1T = 1T=1"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "The first line of the input contains a single integer TTT denoting the number of test cases. The description of TTT test cases follows.\nThe first line of each test case contains two space-separated integers NNN and MMM.\nMMM lines follow. For each iii (1≤i≤M1 \\le i \\le M1≤i≤M), the iii-th of these lines contains three space-separated integers XiX_iXi​, YiY_iYi​ and RiR_iRi​, followed by a space and 2Ri2R_i2Ri​ space-separated integers p1,e1,p2,e2,…,pRi,eRip_1, e_1, p_2, e_2, \\ldots, p_{R_i}, e_{R_i}p1​,e1​,p2​,e2​,…,pRi​​,eRi​​, denoting that Bi=∏r=1RiprerB_i = \\prod_{r=1}^{R_i} p_r^{e_r}Bi​=∏r=1Ri​​prer​​.",
    "outputFormat": "For each test case, print a single line containing one integer ― the number of valid sequences modulo 1,000,000,0071,000,000,0071,000,000,007, or −1-1−1 if there are infinitely many valid sequences.",
